@startuml
title Volaryn | Stored agreement states and explicit transitions
skinparam backgroundColor #101117
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F0FF
skinparam ArrowColor #2CE7B3
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #232333
  BorderColor #AA86F7
  FontColor #F3F0FF
  StartColor #2CE7B3
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #292437
  BorderColor #AA86F7
  FontColor #E7E0F5
}

state Open
state Active
state Exercised
state Cancelled
state Expired
[*] --> Open : create_offer(side)
Open --> Active : activate() or accept_request()\n[opposite actor; now < accept_before\nand now < expires_at; admission passes]
Open --> Cancelled : cancel_offer()\n[creator signs; also allowed after acceptance closes]
Active --> Exercised : exercise()\n[holder signs; now < expires_at; full delivery]
Active --> Expired : reclaim_expired()\n[writer signs; now >= expires_at]
note left of Open
  Deadline passage does not write a new state.
  Open + closed acceptance = unavailable for matching.
  Creator can still refund the original escrow.
end note
note right of Active
  Active + elapsed expiry = awaiting writer reclaim.
  Exercise is disabled, but stored status is still Active.
end note
note bottom of Exercised
  Terminal records remain on chain.
  cleanup_terminal() recovers residual USDC / settlement authority;
  it does not delete Agreement or reopen the right.
end note
@enduml
